From 30ecca608aff13b0e58016ae7e33b084654afd14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rocky <rocky@zeroclaw>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): stream spawn_subagent steps on /ws/chat

A spawn_subagent call made by a turn that streams events now shows the
subagent's run live on the parent's stream. Tool dispatch scopes a
SubagentEventSink (task-local, keyed by the spawn's tool call id) around
the spawn; the child run executes in the same task, so its tool dispatch
mirrors each ToolCall/ToolResult into TurnEvent::Subagent and the spawn
tool brackets the run with Start/End. /ws/chat renders them as
{type:"subagent_event", parent_call_id, event} where event is
subagent_start, a parent-shaped tool_call/tool_result, or subagent_end.
Without a streaming parent (cron, other channels) nothing changes; the
child's behaviour and its result to the parent are untouched.
